  "body": "Split out of #45 (its triage comment, checked on main 8f30bee). Multiple setups work underneath, but in the desktop app a new document cannot reach them:\n\n- The only controls that create a setup - **Create first setup** and **New setup** - are on the Setups page (`pages::setups_page`).\n- The only way to that page is the browser's **Setups** row, and `panes::browser_rows` draws it only once `setup::names` is non-empty - which needs a setup to exist first.\n- The ribbon's Setup group is `[Stock, Origin, Tools, Machine]`, with no Setups cell, and no shortcut targets `UiTarget::Setups`.\n\nSo multiple setups, workholding, the per-setup tool list and **Export setup sheets...** are reachable only by opening a project that already has a setup (#267's \"I have not seen any setup sheets\" is this). The MCP server has no setup tool either.\n\n**Fix:** draw the **Setups** row whenever the Setup section is open (the page already handles no setups: \"No setups in this document ... Create first setup\"), and add a Setups cell to the ribbon's Setup group. The default browser and ribbon change, so the shell pixel snapshots must be regenerated.\n\n**Done means:** in a fresh document the Setups page is reachable from the browser and the ribbon, **Create first setup** works (undoable), pinned by a UI test; snapshots regenerated.\n\nFirst step of the multi-setup chain in #308 (before #315). Part of #45.\n",
